{"nota":"Diccionario ES→EN. El inglés se genera con tools\\i18n.ps1 generar; no editar el .en.js a mano. keep: textos que no se traducen.","lit":{"\u0027 °C (sin pérdidas ni C\u003csub\u003ecal\u003c/sub\u003e).\u003c/p\u003e\u0027":"\" °C (without losses or C\u003csub\u003ecal\u003c/sub\u003e).\u003c/p\u003e\"","\u0027 °C se sumerge en \u0027":"\" °C is immersed in \"","\u0027 °C. Como el calor cedido = el absorbido: \u003cb\u003em₁c₁(T\u003csub\u003ef\u003c/sub\u003e − T₁) = −m₂c₂(T\u003csub\u003ef\u003c/sub\u003e − T₂)\u003c/b\u003e → \u003cb\u003eT\u003csub\u003ef\u003c/sub\u003e = \u0027":"\" °C. Since heat given up = heat absorbed: \u003cb\u003em₁c₁(T\u003csub\u003ef\u003c/sub\u003e − T₁) = −m₂c₂(T\u003csub\u003ef\u003c/sub\u003e − T₂)\u003c/b\u003e → \u003cb\u003eT\u003csub\u003ef\u003c/sub\u003e = \"","\u0027 °C\u003c/b\u003e. El agua tiene un c muy alto: cambia poco su temperatura.\u003c/p\u003e\u0027":"\" °C\u003c/b\u003e. Water has a very high c: its temperature changes little.\u003c/p\u003e\"","\u0027 °C\u003c/div\u003e\u003cdiv class=\"eqline\"\u003e\u003csmall\u003eq cedido por el metal\u003c/small\u003e\u0027":"\" °C\u003c/div\u003e\u003cdiv class=\\\"eqline\\\"\u003e\u003csmall\u003eq given up by the metal\u003c/small\u003e\"","\u0027 · endotérmica\u0027":"\" · endothermic\"","\u0027 · exotérmica\u0027":"\" · exothermic\"","\u0027 g de \u0027":"\" g of \"","\u0027 g de agua (c = 4,18) a \u0027":"\" g of water (c = 4.18) at \"","\u0027 g de agua · \u0027":"\" g of water · \"","\u0027 kJ ✓ (sistema aislado)\u0027":"\" kJ ✓ (isolated system)\"","\u0027 kJ/mol) con 0,050 mol en 100 mL: ΔT = \u0027":"\" kJ/mol) with 0.050 mol in 100 mL: ΔT = \"","\u0027 kJ/mol\u003c/b\u003e. Es el mismo número que se obtiene por la ley de Hess en el ciclo con elementos.\u003c/p\u003e\u0027":"\" kJ/mol\u003c/b\u003e. It is the same number obtained by Hess\u0027s law in the cycle with elements.\u003c/p\u003e\"","\u0027 kJ/mol\u003c/div\u003e\u003cdiv class=\"eqline\"\u003e\u003csmall\u003eTipo\u003c/small\u003e\u0027":"\" kJ/mol\u003c/div\u003e\u003cdiv class=\\\"eqline\\\"\u003e\u003csmall\u003eType\u003c/small\u003e\"","\u0027 kJ/mol\u003c/div\u003e\u003cdiv class=\"eqline\"\u003e\u003csmall\u003eΔT del calorímetro\u003c/small\u003e\u0027":"\" kJ/mol\u003c/div\u003e\u003cdiv class=\\\"eqline\\\"\u003e\u003csmall\u003eΔT of the calorimeter\u003c/small\u003e\"","\u0027 mol · \u0027":"\" mol · \"","\u0027¿Cuánto calor absorben 100 g de agua al calentarse de 20 °C a 30 °C? (c = 4,18 J/g·°C)\u0027":"\"How much heat do 100 g of water absorb when heated from 20 °C to 30 °C? (c = 4.18 J/g·°C)\"","\u0027\u003c/table\u003e\u003cdiv class=\"calc-step\"\u003e2 · Calor y ΔT\u003c/div\u003e\u003ctable class=\"calc-table\"\u003e\u0027":"\"\u003c/table\u003e\u003cdiv class=\\\"calc-step\\\"\u003e2 · Heat and ΔT\u003c/div\u003e\u003ctable class=\\\"calc-table\\\"\u003e\"","\u0027\u003c/table\u003e\u003cdiv class=\"calc-step\"\u003e2 · Temperatura final\u003c/div\u003e\u003ctable class=\"calc-table\"\u003e\u0027":"\"\u003c/table\u003e\u003cdiv class=\\\"calc-step\\\"\u003e2 · Final temperature\u003c/div\u003e\u003ctable class=\\\"calc-table\\\"\u003e\"","\u0027\u003c/table\u003e\u003cdiv class=\"calc-step\"\u003e3 · Problema inverso\u003c/div\u003e\u003ctable class=\"calc-table\"\u003e\u0027":"\"\u003c/table\u003e\u003cdiv class=\\\"calc-step\\\"\u003e3 · Inverse problem\u003c/div\u003e\u003ctable class=\\\"calc-table\\\"\u003e\"","\u0027\u003c/table\u003e\u003cp class=\"muted small\"\u003eInvertir una reacción cambia el signo de ΔH; multiplicarla por n multiplica ΔH por n.\u003c/p\u003e\u0027":"\"\u003c/table\u003e\u003cp class=\\\"muted small\\\"\u003eReversing a reaction changes the sign of ΔH; multiplying it by n multiplies ΔH by n.\u003c/p\u003e\"","\u0027\u003cb\u003eHess\u003c/b\u003e: ΔH no depende del camino (función de estado).\u0027":"\"\u003cb\u003eHess\u003c/b\u003e: ΔH does not depend on the path (state function).\"","\u0027\u003cb\u003eq = m·c·ΔT\u003c/b\u003e; q \u0026gt; 0 absorbe, q \u0026lt; 0 libera.\u0027":"\"\u003cb\u003eq = m·c·ΔT\u003c/b\u003e; q \u0026gt; 0 absorbs, q \u0026lt; 0 releases.\"","\u0027\u003cb\u003eΔH = q\u003csub\u003ep\u003c/sub\u003e/n\u003c/b\u003e; exotérmica ΔH \u0026lt; 0, endotérmica ΔH \u0026gt; 0.\u0027":"\"\u003cb\u003eΔH = q\u003csub\u003ep\u003c/sub\u003e/n\u003c/b\u003e; exothermic ΔH \u0026lt; 0, endothermic ΔH \u0026gt; 0.\"","\u0027\u003cb\u003eΔH° = ΣΔH°f(productos) − ΣΔH°f(reactivos)\u003c/b\u003e; ΔH°f de un elemento = 0.\u0027":"\"\u003cb\u003eΔH° = ΣΔH°f(products) − ΣΔH°f(reactants)\u003c/b\u003e; ΔH°f of an element = 0.\"","\u0027\u003cdiv class=\"card-kicker\"\u003eCalorimetría a presión constante\u003c/div\u003e\u003cdiv class=\"calc-step\"\u003e1 · Capacidad calorífica total\u003c/div\u003e\u003ctable class=\"calc-table\"\u003e\u0027":"\"\u003cdiv class=\\\"card-kicker\\\"\u003eConstant-pressure calorimetry\u003c/div\u003e\u003cdiv class=\\\"calc-step\\\"\u003e1 · Total heat capacity\u003c/div\u003e\u003ctable class=\\\"calc-table\\\"\u003e\"","\u0027\u003cdiv class=\"card-kicker\"\u003eCombustión de \u0027":"\"\u003cdiv class=\\\"card-kicker\\\"\u003eCombustion of \"","\u0027\u003cdiv class=\"card-kicker\"\u003eEquilibrio térmico\u003c/div\u003e\u003cdiv class=\"calc-step\"\u003e1 · Capacidades caloríficas (m·c)\u003c/div\u003e\u003ctable class=\"calc-table\"\u003e\u0027":"\"\u003cdiv class=\\\"card-kicker\\\"\u003eThermal equilibrium\u003c/div\u003e\u003cdiv class=\\\"calc-step\\\"\u003e1 · Heat capacities (m·c)\u003c/div\u003e\u003ctable class=\\\"calc-table\\\"\u003e\"","\u0027\u003cdiv class=\"card-kicker\"\u003eLey de Hess\u003c/div\u003e\u003ctable class=\"calc-table\"\u003e\u0027":"\"\u003cdiv class=\\\"card-kicker\\\"\u003eHess\u0027s law\u003c/div\u003e\u003ctable class=\\\"calc-table\\\"\u003e\"","\u0027\u003cdiv class=\"eqline\"\u003e\u003csmall\u003eT final (equilibrio)\u003c/small\u003e\u0027":"\"\u003cdiv class=\\\"eqline\\\"\u003e\u003csmall\u003eFinal T (equilibrium)\u003c/small\u003e\"","\u0027\u003cdiv class=\"eqline\"\u003e\u003csmall\u003eΔH reacción\u003c/small\u003e\u0027":"\"\u003cdiv class=\\\"eqline\\\"\u003e\u003csmall\u003eΔH reaction\u003c/small\u003e\"","\u0027\u003cdiv class=\"eqline\"\u003e\u003csmall\u003eΔH total\u003c/small\u003e−393,5 kJ\u003c/div\u003e\u003cdiv class=\"eqline\"\u003e\u003csmall\u003eCamino\u003c/small\u003e−110,5 + (−283,0)\u003c/div\u003e\u0027":"\"\u003cdiv class=\\\"eqline\\\"\u003e\u003csmall\u003eTotal ΔH\u003c/small\u003e−393.5 kJ\u003c/div\u003e\u003cdiv class=\\\"eqline\\\"\u003e\u003csmall\u003ePath\u003c/small\u003e−110.5 + (−283.0)\u003c/div\u003e\"","\u0027\u003cp class=\"muted small\"\u003eSe supone calor específico de la disolución 4,18 J/g·°C, densidad 1 g/mL, sin pérdidas de calor. Entalpías estándar: valores de tablas (kJ/mol).\u003c/p\u003e\u0027":"\"\u003cp class=\\\"muted small\\\"\u003eThe specific heat of the solution is assumed to be 4.18 J/g·°C, density 1 g/mL, no heat losses. Standard enthalpies: table values (kJ/mol).\u003c/p\u003e\"","\u0027\u003cp\u003eEl \u003cb\u003esistema\u003c/b\u003e es la parte que estudiamos (el bloque de metal, la reacción) y los \u003cb\u003ealrededores\u003c/b\u003e todo lo demás (el agua del calorímetro). El calor \u003cb\u003eq\u003c/b\u003e fluye de lo caliente a lo frío.\u003c/p\u003e\u003cp\u003eConvención: \u003cb\u003eq \u0026gt; 0\u003c/b\u003e si el sistema \u003cb\u003eabsorbe\u003c/b\u003e calor (endotérmico) y \u003cb\u003eq \u0026lt; 0\u003c/b\u003e si lo \u003cb\u003elibera\u003c/b\u003e (exotérmico). En un sistema aislado, q\u003csub\u003esistema\u003c/sub\u003e + q\u003csub\u003ealrededores\u003c/sub\u003e = 0.\u003c/p\u003e\u0027":"\"\u003cp\u003eThe \u003cb\u003esystem\u003c/b\u003e is the part we study (the metal block, the reaction) and the \u003cb\u003esurroundings\u003c/b\u003e everything else (the calorimeter water). Heat \u003cb\u003eq\u003c/b\u003e flows from hot to cold.\u003c/p\u003e\u003cp\u003eConvention: \u003cb\u003eq \u0026gt; 0\u003c/b\u003e if the system \u003cb\u003eabsorbs\u003c/b\u003e heat (endothermic) and \u003cb\u003eq \u0026lt; 0\u003c/b\u003e if it \u003cb\u003ereleases\u003c/b\u003e it (exothermic). In an isolated system, q\u003csub\u003esystem\u003c/sub\u003e + q\u003csub\u003esurroundings\u003c/sub\u003e = 0.\u003c/p\u003e\"","\u0027\u003cp\u003eEl calor intercambiado es \u003cb\u003eq = m · c · ΔT\u003c/b\u003e. Un bloque de \u0027":"\"\u003cp\u003eThe heat exchanged is \u003cb\u003eq = m · c · ΔT\u003c/b\u003e. A block at \"","\u0027\u003cp\u003eEn un calorímetro a presión constante, \u003cb\u003eq\u003csub\u003ereacción\u003c/sub\u003e = −(m·c + C\u003csub\u003ecal\u003c/sub\u003e)·ΔT\u003c/b\u003e y \u003cb\u003eΔH = q / n\u003c/b\u003e. Para la neutralización HCl + NaOH (ΔH = \u0027":"\"\u003cp\u003eIn a constant-pressure calorimeter, \u003cb\u003eq\u003csub\u003ereaction\u003c/sub\u003e = −(m·c + C\u003csub\u003ecal\u003c/sub\u003e)·ΔT\u003c/b\u003e and \u003cb\u003eΔH = q / n\u003c/b\u003e. For the neutralization HCl + NaOH (ΔH = \"","\u0027\u003cp\u003eLa \u003cb\u003eentalpía\u003c/b\u003e H es el calor a presión constante. \u003cb\u003eΔH = H\u003csub\u003eproductos\u003c/sub\u003e − H\u003csub\u003ereactivos\u003c/sub\u003e\u003c/b\u003e. En una reacción \u003cb\u003eexotérmica\u003c/b\u003e (ΔH \u0026lt; 0, p. ej. neutralización −57,1 kJ/mol) la energía baja y el entorno se calienta; en una \u003cb\u003eendotérmica\u003c/b\u003e (ΔH \u0026gt; 0, p. ej. NH₄NO₃ disolviéndose +25,7 kJ/mol) sube y el entorno se enfría.\u003c/p\u003e\u0027":"\"\u003cp\u003e\u003cb\u003eEnthalpy\u003c/b\u003e H is the heat at constant pressure. \u003cb\u003eΔH = H\u003csub\u003eproducts\u003c/sub\u003e − H\u003csub\u003ereactants\u003c/sub\u003e\u003c/b\u003e. In an \u003cb\u003eexothermic\u003c/b\u003e reaction (ΔH \u0026lt; 0, e.g. neutralization −57.1 kJ/mol) the energy drops and the surroundings warm up; in an \u003cb\u003eendothermic\u003c/b\u003e one (ΔH \u0026gt; 0, e.g. NH₄NO₃ dissolving +25.7 kJ/mol) it rises and the surroundings cool down.\u003c/p\u003e\"","\u0027\u003cp\u003eLa entalpía es una \u003cb\u003efunción de estado\u003c/b\u003e: da igual el camino. C(s) + ½O₂ → CO (−110,5) y CO + ½O₂ → CO₂ (−283,0) suman \u003cb\u003e−393,5 kJ\u003c/b\u003e, igual que la reacción directa C + O₂ → CO₂. Al \u003cb\u003einvertir\u003c/b\u003e una reacción cambia el signo de ΔH; al \u003cb\u003emultiplicarla\u003c/b\u003e, ΔH se multiplica.\u003c/p\u003e\u0027":"\"\u003cp\u003eEnthalpy is a \u003cb\u003estate function\u003c/b\u003e: the path does not matter. C(s) + ½O₂ → CO (−110.5) and CO + ½O₂ → CO₂ (−283.0) add up to \u003cb\u003e−393.5 kJ\u003c/b\u003e, the same as the direct reaction C + O₂ → CO₂. When a reaction is \u003cb\u003ereversed\u003c/b\u003e the sign of ΔH changes; when it is \u003cb\u003emultiplied\u003c/b\u003e, ΔH is multiplied.\u003c/p\u003e\"","\u0027\u003cp\u003eUsando elementos (ΔH°f = 0) como referencia: para la combustión del metano, ΔH° = [−393,5 + 2(−285,8)] − [−74,8] = \u003cb\u003e\u0027":"\"\u003cp\u003eUsing elements (ΔH°f = 0) as reference: for the combustion of methane, ΔH° = [−393.5 + 2(−285.8)] − [−74.8] = \u003cb\u003e\"","\u0027\u003csmall\u003ec(agua) = 4,18 J/g·°C · presión constante\u003c/small\u003e\u0027":"\"\u003csmall\u003ec(water) = 4.18 J/g·°C · constant pressure\u003c/small\u003e\"","\u0027«Experimento» (metal en agua, entalpía, ley de Hess o ΔH°f) y sus datos: masas y temperaturas, reacción, n, volumen, capacidad calorífica del calorímetro y combustible.\u0027":"\u0027the experiment (metal in water, enthalpy, Hess’s law or ΔH°f) and its data: masses and temperatures, reaction, n, volume, calorimeter heat capacity and fuel.\u0027","\u0027▶ Iniciar\u0027":"\"▶ Start\"","\u00270,418 kJ\u0027":"\"0.418 kJ\"","\u0027−110,5 kJ\u0027":"\"−110.5 kJ\"","\u0027−1180,3 kJ\u0027":"\"−1180.3 kJ\"","\u0027−172,5 kJ\u0027":"\"−172.5 kJ\"","\u0027−283,0 kJ\u0027":"\"−283.0 kJ\"","\u0027−393,5 kJ\u0027":"\"−393.5 kJ\"","\u00274,18 kJ\u0027":"\"4.18 kJ\"","\u002741,8 kJ\u0027":"\"41.8 kJ\"","\u0027−604,5 kJ\u0027":"\"−604.5 kJ\"","\u0027−890,3 kJ\u0027":"\"−890.3 kJ\"","\u0027Agua\u0027":"\"Water\"","\u0027Al disolver NH₄NO₃ en agua (ΔH = +25,7 kJ/mol) la disolución…\u0027":"\"When NH₄NO₃ is dissolved in water (ΔH = +25.7 kJ/mol) the solution…\"","\u0027aluminio\u0027":"\"aluminium\"","\u0027Azul\u0027":"\"Blue\"","\u0027Barras a la izquierda del cero: exotérmicas (liberan calor); a la derecha: endotérmicas.\u0027":"\"Bars to the left of zero: exothermic (release heat); to the right: endothermic.\"","\u0027C calorímetro\u0027":"\"C calorimeter\"","\u0027C(graf) + O₂(g)\u0027":"\"C(graphite) + O₂(g)\"","\u0027C(s) + ½O₂ → CO tiene ΔH = −110,5 kJ y CO + ½O₂ → CO₂ tiene ΔH = −283,0 kJ. ¿Cuál es ΔH de C(s) + O₂ → CO₂?\u0027":"\"C(s) + ½O₂ → CO has ΔH = −110.5 kJ and CO + ½O₂ → CO₂ has ΔH = −283.0 kJ. What is ΔH of C(s) + O₂ → CO₂?\"","\u0027C(s) + O₂ → CO₂ = \u003cb\u003e−393,5 kJ\u003c/b\u003e\u0027":"\"C(s) + O₂ → CO₂ = \u003cb\u003e−393.5 kJ\u003c/b\u003e\"","\u0027CaCl₂(s) → Ca²⁺(ac) + 2 Cl⁻(ac)\u0027":"\u0027CaCl₂(s) → Ca²⁺(aq) + 2 Cl⁻(aq)\u0027","\u0027Cálculo\u0027":"\"Calculation\"","\u0027calor absorbido / T baja\u0027":"\"heat absorbed / low T\"","\u0027Calor cedido = calor absorbido en un sistema aislado.\u0027":"\"Heat given up = heat absorbed in an isolated system.\"","\u0027Calor específico\u0027":"\"Specific heat\"","\u0027calor liberado / T alta\u0027":"\"heat released / high T\"","\u0027Calorimetría\u0027":"\"Calorimetry\"","\u0027Calorímetro\u0027":"\"Calorimeter\"","\u0027Cambia de signo y se duplica\u0027":"\"Changes sign and doubles\"","\u0027cobre\u0027":"\"copper\"","\u0027Combustible\u0027":"\"Fuel\"","\u0027Combustible (ΔH°f)\u0027":"\"Fuel (ΔH°f)\"","\u0027combustión\u0027":"\"combustion\"","\u0027Combustión de \u0027":"\"Combustion of \"","\u0027Con ΔH°f calcula el ΔH de combustión de un combustible y compáralo con el panel.\u0027":"\u0027With ΔH°f work out the combustion ΔH of a fuel and compare it with the panel.\u0027","\u0027Con ΔH°f(CO₂) = −393,5, ΔH°f(H₂O,l) = −285,8 y ΔH°f(CH₄) = −74,8 kJ/mol, ¿cuál es ΔH° de CH₄ + 2 O₂ → CO₂ + 2 H₂O(l)?\u0027":"\"With ΔH°f(CO₂) = −393.5, ΔH°f(H₂O,l) = −285.8 and ΔH°f(CH₄) = −74.8 kJ/mol, what is ΔH° of CH₄ + 2 O₂ → CO₂ + 2 H₂O(l)?\"","\u0027Conclusión\u0027":"\"Conclusion\"","\u0027Controles\u0027":"\u0027Controls\u0027","\u0027curvas T(t) y comparación de ΔH.\u0027":"\"T(t) curves and ΔH comparison.\"","\u0027Diagrama\u0027":"\"Diagram\"","\u0027Diagramas\u0027":"\"Diagrams\"","\u0027disolución de \u0027":"\"dissolution of \"","\u0027disolución de CaCl₂\u0027":"\"CaCl₂ dissolution\"","\u0027disolución de NaOH\u0027":"\"NaOH dissolution\"","\u0027disolución de NH₄NO₃\u0027":"\"NH₄NO₃ dissolution\"","\u0027Ebulle\u0027":"\"Boils\"","\u0027El sistema libera calor (q \u003c 0, ΔH \u003c 0) y lo cede a los alrededores, que se calientan.\u0027":"\"The system releases heat (q \u003c 0, ΔH \u003c 0) and gives it to the surroundings, which warm up.\"","\u0027Elementos (ΔH°f = 0)\u0027":"\"Elements (ΔH°f = 0)\"","\u0027Elige el experimento en «Lab» o sigue la lección. «Iniciar» anima el proceso.\u0027":"\"Choose the experiment in “Lab” or follow the lesson. “Start” animates the process.\"","\u0027En «Ley de Hess» compara el camino directo con el de dos pasos: el ΔH total es el mismo.\u0027":"\u0027In Hess’s law compare the direct path with the two-step one: the total ΔH is the same.\u0027","\u0027En «Metal en agua» sumerge el metal caliente: el calor que cede es igual al que gana el agua.\u0027":"\u0027In metal in water drop the hot metal in: the heat it gives off equals the heat the water gains.\u0027","\u0027En el calorímetro, ΔT mide el calor de la reacción\u0027":"\"In the calorimeter, ΔT measures the heat of the reaction\"","\u0027En una reacción exotérmica, ¿qué signo tiene ΔH y qué le pasa al entorno?\u0027":"\"In an exothermic reaction, what sign does ΔH have and what happens to the surroundings?\"","\u0027endotérmica\u0027":"\"endothermic\"","\u0027endotérmica: el agua se enfría\u0027":"\"endothermic: the water cools down\"","\u0027Entalpía\u0027":"\"Enthalpy\"","\u0027Entalpías de formación\u0027":"\"Enthalpies of formation\"","\u0027etanol\u0027":"\"ethanol\"","\u0027Exo y endotérmico\u0027":"\"Exo- and endothermic\"","\u0027exotérmica\u0027":"\"exothermic\"","\u0027exotérmica: el agua se calienta\u0027":"\"exothermic: the water warms up\"","\u0027Experimento\u0027":"\"Experiment\"","\u0027Frontal\u0027":"\"Front\"","\u0027glucosa\u0027":"\"glucose\"","\u0027Gráficos\u0027":"\"Graphs\"","\u0027hierro\u0027":"\"iron\"","\u0027La energía se transfiere como calor entre sistema y alrededores\u0027":"\"Energy is transferred as heat between system and surroundings\"","\u0027La neutralización HCl + NaOH tiene ΔH = −57,1 kJ/mol. Con 0,050 mol en 100 g de disolución (c = 4,18 J/g·°C, sin pérdidas), ¿cuánto sube la temperatura?\u0027":"\"The neutralization HCl + NaOH has ΔH = −57.1 kJ/mol. With 0.050 mol in 100 g of solution (c = 4.18 J/g·°C, no losses), how much does the temperature rise?\"","\u0027la temperatura del agua (termómetro) cambia según el calor intercambiado; el halo rojo/azul indica liberación/absorción.\u0027":"\"the water temperature (thermometer) changes according to the heat exchanged; the red/blue halo indicates release/absorption.\"","\u0027Ley de Hess\u0027":"\"Hess\u0027s law\"","\u0027Ley de Hess: se suman las ecuaciones y sus ΔH: −110,5 + (−283,0) = −393,5 kJ.\u0027":"\"Hess\u0027s law: the equations and their ΔH are added: −110.5 + (−283.0) = −393.5 kJ.\"","\u0027Libre\u0027":"\"Free\"","\u0027los niveles de entalpía muestran exo/endotermia, ley de Hess y entalpías de formación.\u0027":"\"the enthalpy levels show exo/endothermicity, Hess\u0027s law and enthalpies of formation.\"","\u0027m agua\u0027":"\"m water\"","\u0027m·c (disolución)\u0027":"\"m·c (solution)\"","\u0027Metal en agua\u0027":"\"Metal in water\"","\u0027Metal en agua: ambas curvas convergen a T\u003csub\u003ef\u003c/sub\u003e. Calorímetro: la temperatura sube (exotérmica) o baja (endotérmica). El punto marca el progreso.\u0027":"\"Metal in water: both curves converge to T\u003csub\u003ef\u003c/sub\u003e. Calorimeter: the temperature rises (exothermic) or falls (endothermic). The dot marks the progress.\"","\u0027metano\u0027":"\"methane\"","\u0027Modo\u0027":"\"Mode\"","\u0027NaOH(s) → Na⁺(ac) + OH⁻(ac)\u0027":"\u0027NaOH(s) → Na⁺(aq) + OH⁻(aq)\u0027","\u0027neutralización\u0027":"\"neutralization\"","\u0027NH₄NO₃(s) → NH₄⁺(ac) + NO₃⁻(ac)\u0027":"\u0027NH₄NO₃(s) → NH₄⁺(aq) + NO₃⁻(aq)\u0027","\u0027No cambia\u0027":"\"Does not change\"","\u0027No cambia de temperatura\u0027":"\"Does not change temperature\"","\u0027Panel de control\u0027":"\"Control panel\"","\u0027plomo\u0027":"\"lead\"","\u0027Por gramo\u0027":"\"Per gram\"","\u0027Proceso endotérmico: absorbe calor de la disolución (y el entorno), que se enfría.\u0027":"\"Endothermic process: it absorbs heat from the solution (and the surroundings), which cools down.\"","\u0027Productos\u0027":"\"Products\"","\u0027Progreso\u0027":"\"Progress\"","\u0027propano\u0027":"\"propane\"","\u0027q = 57,1 × 0,050 = 2,855 kJ = 2855 J; ΔT = 2855/(100 × 4,18) = 6,8 °C.\u0027":"\"q = 57.1 × 0.050 = 2.855 kJ = 2855 J; ΔT = 2855/(100 × 4.18) = 6.8 °C.\"","\u0027q = m·c·ΔT = 100 × 4,18 × 10 = 4180 J = 4,18 kJ.\u0027":"\"q = m·c·ΔT = 100 × 4.18 × 10 = 4180 J = 4.18 kJ.\"","\u0027q agua\u0027":"\"q water\"","\u0027q agua = \u0027":"\"q water = \"","\u0027q reacción\u0027":"\"q reaction\"","\u0027q reacción = \u0027":"\"q reaction = \"","\u0027Reacción\u0027":"\"Reaction\"","\u0027Reacción (calorímetro / entalpía)\u0027":"\"Reaction (calorimeter / enthalpy)\"","\u0027Reactivos\u0027":"\"Reactants\"","\u0027Reiniciar\u0027":"\"Restart\"","\u0027resolución paso a paso del experimento actual.\u0027":"\"step-by-step solution 